WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:05.634
♪♪

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.701
Narrator: CANDIED FRUIT
AND FRUIT JELLIES

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.634
ARE MIDDLE EASTERN IN ORIGIN

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:12.200
AND SPREAD TO EUROPE
AROUND THE 12th CENTURY.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.434
THIS REGION OF FRANCE
HAS BEEN PRODUCING THEM

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.434
SINCE THE 15th CENTURY.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.167
WHEN WARS BLOCKED ACCESS
TO CANE SUGAR,

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.934
FRUIT FARMERS BEGAN
PLANTING SUGAR BEETS

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.367
TO PRESERVE THIS
CONFECTIONERY TRADITION.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:31.133
THIS COMPANY IN FRANCE HAS BEEN
CATERING TO PEOPLE'S SWEET TOOTH

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.901
SINCE 1880 WITH ITS GIFT BOXES

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:39.334
CONTAINING TRADITIONAL CANDIED
FRUIT AND FRUIT JELLIES.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:43.300
TO MAKE CANDIED FRUIT, A MASTER
CONFECTIONER BOILS FRESH FRUIT

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.267
FOR MANY HOURS
TO SOFTEN THE FIBERS.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:50.234
THIS PROCESS WILL LATER HELP
SUGAR TO PENETRATE THE FRUIT.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:53.968
HE POKES THE FRUIT TO SEE
IF IT'S READY.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.400
BOILING TIME VARIES
FROM ONE HOUR FOR APRICOTS

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.801
TO EIGHT HOURS FOR CHESTNUTS.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:03.968
CITRUS FRUITS ARE SLICED
BEFORE BOILING.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.968
AFTER BOILING, THE MORE
FRAGILE TYPES OF FRUIT,

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:10.133
SUCH AS APRICOTS,
PEARS AND CLEMENTINES,

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.434
GO INTO LARGE HOT-AIR
DEHYDRATORS

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.400
FOR UP TO THREE WEEKS.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.934
EVERY DAY, THE MASTER
CONFECTIONER REPLACES

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:19.601
THE EVAPORATED WATER
WITH SUGAR SYRUP,

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:23.534
WHICH CONCENTRATES OVER TIME.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:26.634
FOR LESS FRAGILE FRUITS,
THE TECHNIQUE IS DIFFERENT.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:30.901
WORKERS HEAT THEM IN VATS OF
SUGAR SYRUP FOR ABOUT 10 DAYS.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:34.567
THE MOISTURE EVAPORATES,
AND THE SYRUP CONCENTRATES.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.767
THE FACTORY SELLS
WHOLE CANDIED FRUITS

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.868
LIKE THIS COLLECTION
OF CLEMENTINES,

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.634
APRICOTS, PEARS, FIGS,
AND PLUMS,

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.501
TO GOURMET FOOD SHOPS,

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:49.267
WHICH SELL THEM BY THE PIECE
OR IN ELEGANT,

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.534
PRIVATE-LABEL GIFT BOXES.

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:56.968
♪♪

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.033
WHOLE CANDIED FRUIT
ARE ALSO POPULAR

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:02.801
FOR DESIGNING
EDIBLE ARRANGEMENTS.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:06.100
MAKING FRUIT JELLIES
IS A DIFFERENT PROCESS.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.467
THE RECIPE COMBINES FRUIT PULP,

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:10.801
MAKING UP MORE THAN
50% OF THE MIXTURE,

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.734
WITH POWDERED SUGAR,
LIQUID GLUCOSE,

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:15.534
A FORM OF PLANT SUGAR,

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:18.033
PECTIN TO MAKE
THE MIX GELATINOUS,

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.667
AND NATURAL FRUIT FLAVORING.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.300
A WORKER BOILS DOWN THE MIX
FOR A HALF-HOUR

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.033
TO CONCENTRATE THE SUGAR,

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.501
THEN ADDS MORE FRUIT FLAVORING.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.734
AS THE MIX CONTINUES TO COOK,

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:33.000
SHE DRAWS SAMPLES TO MEASURE
THE SUGAR CONTENT.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.701
SHE DOES THIS UNTIL THE MIX

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:39.167
HITS ITS TARGET
CONCENTRATION OF 78%.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.300
ANOTHER WORKER POURS
THE BATCH FROM THE POT

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.868
INTO A LARGE PITCHER,

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.734
THEN INTO A SQUARE
STAINLESS-STEEL MOLD.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.934
IT TAKES THE JELLY A DAY TO SET.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:58.100
ONCE SET, A WORKER REMOVES IT
FROM THE MOLD --

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.934
THIS ONE'S
A DIFFERENT FLAVOR --

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:05.000
AND COATS IT WITH CRYSTALLIZED
SUGAR TO PRESERVE IT.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.767
THE WORKER THEN LAYS
THE JELLY SQUARE ON A CUTTER

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.701
THE COMPANY CALLS A GUITAR

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:13.400
BECAUSE ITS STEEL WIRES
LOOK LIKE GUITAR STRINGS.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.300
THE WIRES CUT ONCE IN EACH
DIRECTION TO MAKE CUBES.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.367
THEN, ANOTHER WORKER APPLIES
A SECOND COATING OF SUGAR.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.000
IN ADDITION TO THIS
SMALL-BATCH PRODUCTION,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.467
THE FACTORY
HAS ONE AUTOMATED MACHINE,

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.667
WHICH MAKES FRUIT JELLIES

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:30.701
IN A VARIETY OF GEOMETRIC
OR FRUIT SHAPES

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.868
CREATED BY TEMPLATES
MADE OF PLASTER.

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:40.133
THIS PROCESS IS MUCH FASTER
THAN THE HANDMADE APPROACH.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:44.801
FIRST, THE MACHINE
MAKES A BED OF STARCH.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.467
THEN IT PRESSES
THE PLASTER FORM INTO THE BED

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.968
TO CREATE MOLD CAVITIES.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:54.501
♪♪

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.400
THE NEXT STATION FILLS
THE CAVITIES

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.968
WITH HOT LIQUID FRUIT JELLY.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:02.934
THEN, THE MOLDS
ARE SET ASIDE FOR A DAY.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:08.000
THE STARCH ABSORBS THE RESIDUAL
MOISTURE AS THE JELLY SETS.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.534
THE NEXT DAY,
WORKERS LOAD THE MOLDS

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.300
ON TOP OF THE SAME MACHINE,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.334
WHICH FLIPS THEM TO DUMP OUT
THE JELLIES.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:18.734
THE JELLIES TUMBLE DOWN
A VIBRATING CONVEYOR BELT.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:22.267
THE STARCH SHAKES OFF
WITH EACH BOUNCE.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.167
THEN THEY PASS
UNDER A SPINNING BRUSH,

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.968
WHICH REMOVES
ANY REMAINING STARCH.

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:30.834
THE CONVEYOR MOVES THEM
INTO A ROTATING DRUM,

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.801
WHICH SHOWERS THEM WITH SUGAR.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.934
ON THE PACKAGING LINE,
A SLOW CONVEYOR BELT MOVES

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.501
RETAIL BOXES
IN FRONT OF A ROW OF WORKERS.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:45.000
EACH WORKER IS RESPONSIBLE
FOR A SINGLE FLAVOR.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.234
WHILE PLACING THE REQUIRED
NUMBER OF FRUIT JELLIES

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.334
IN THE BOX,

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:51.334
SHE ALSO PERFORMS
A QUALITY CONTROL CHECK,

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.667
REMOVING AND REPLACING
ANY THAT ARE MISSHAPEN.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.467
THIS ENSURES THAT THESE
TRADITIONAL FRUIT JELLIES

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.801
LOOK AS GOOD AS THEY TASTE.

